          "en": "(1) An amendment to the articles of association of a Company that has been declared bankrupt may not be made, except with the approval of the receiver.\n\n(2) The approval of the receiver as referred to in paragraph (1) is attached to the application for approval or the notification of the amendment to the articles of association to the Minister.\n\nParagraph (1) The approval of the receiver is obtained before the resolution on the amendment to the articles of association is taken. This is intended to avoid the possibility of rejection by the receiver resulting in the resolution on the amendment to the articles of association becoming void.\n\nParagraph (2) Sufficiently clear."
